1. What you may do

   a. View this repository and download it.

   b. Run it on computers you control, as published, for the sole purpose of
      evaluating Claude Code's Code Mode for yourself or within your own
      organisation. Using the settings the Benchmark Guide documents, and making
      the small changes needed for it to run on your system, counts as running
      it as published.

   c. Publish the results you obtain, and quote short passages of the
      documentation for comment or review, provided you credit
      "Claude Code Code Mode Benchmark, Bicameral, LLC" and link to
      https://github.com/Bicameral-AI/claude-code-mode-benchmark.

2. What you may not do without prior written permission from Bicameral, LLC

   a. Copy, redistribute, sublicense, rent or sell this repository or any
      substantial part of it, including its tasks, prompts, data, scripts,
      documentation and diagrams.

   b. Change it or add to it: new or altered tests, prompts, data, scoring or
      measures. To suggest a test or an extension, open an issue as described
      at the end of this notice.

   c. Use its scripts, tasks, prompts, data or documentation, in whole or in
      part, as the basis for testing anything other than Claude Code's Code
      Mode: for example another feature, another tool, or a comparison of
      models with each other. If you want to do that, open an issue that says
      what you want to test and how you would use this repository. Permission
      may be granted in writing; opening an issue is a request, not permission.

   d. Publish a modified version of it, or present it, or anything derived
      from it, as your own benchmark or under another name.

   e. Include it or any part of it in a product, a service, a dataset or
      another benchmark, whether or not you charge for it.

   f. Use its tasks, prompts or data to train a machine learning model.

   g. Remove or alter this notice or any copyright notice in the repository.

